{"claims":[{"excerpt":"How GRACE Follow-On Tracks Changes in Earth’s Water","claim":"GRACE Follow-On tracks changes in Earth's water.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The mission follows changes involving groundwater, lakes and rivers, soil moisture, glaciers, ice sheets and changes in sea level attributable to water added to the oceans.","narrative":"Explain how GRACE Follow-On’s two satellites use changes in the distance between them to help investigate water movement on Earth.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The title concisely describes the mission's tracking of changes involving water.","materiality":"This is the piece's central subject."},{"excerpt":"GRACE Follow-On consists of two satellites that follow one another about 137 miles (220 kilometers) apart.","claim":"GRACE Follow-On consists of two satellites that follow one another about 137 miles (220 kilometers) apart.","category":"quantity","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Twin satellites follow each other about 137 miles or 220 kilometers apart.","narrative":"GRACE Follow-On consists of two satellites that follow one another about 137 miles (220 kilometers) apart.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The satellite count and approximate separation match the source, with equivalent unit conversions.","materiality":"Provides factual context for how the mission works."},{"excerpt":"As the pair approaches a larger mass concentration, gravity affects the leading satellite first, initially pulling it farther from the trailing satellite.","claim":"As the pair approaches a larger mass concentration, gravity acts on the leading satellite before the trailing satellite and initially pulls the leading satellite farther away.","category":"cause","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"As the pair approaches a larger mass concentration, stronger gravity acts on the leading satellite first, initially pulling it farther from the trailing one.","narrative":"As the pair passes a larger mass concentration, gravity affects the leading satellite first, initially increasing its distance from the trailing satellite.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The order and initial direction of the effect match the source. Omitting “stronger” does not change the stated relationship.","materiality":"Explains the physical basis of the changing separation."},{"excerpt":"The changing distance between the satellites is a measurement scientists use to infer shifts in mass.","claim":"Scientists use the changing distance between the satellites as a measurement to infer shifts in mass.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The changing inter-satellite distance is a raw measurement used to infer shifts in mass.","narrative":"That changing separation is a measurement used to infer shifts in mass.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The measurement and inference are accurately described; “raw” is omitted without changing the claim.","materiality":"This is the central measurement-to-inference relationship."},{"excerpt":"It is not a direct measurement of groundwater;","claim":"The satellite-distance measurement is not a direct measurement of groundwater.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The changing inter-satellite distance is a raw measurement used to infer shifts in mass.","narrative":"Do not describe the separation measurement as a change in altitude or as a direct image or measurement of groundwater.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source identifies distance as a measurement used to infer mass shifts, not as a direct groundwater measurement.","materiality":"Clarifies what the instrument measures and avoids overstating its directness."},{"excerpt":"the inferred mass changes can help reveal water movement on Earth.","claim":"Inferred changes in mass can help reveal water movement on Earth.","category":"in